00:13:33.340 --> 00:13:43.180
I wanted to come in with like an interesting tidbit that we could throw in there if there was ever a moment where we weren't covering something about the show.

308
00:13:43.300 --> 00:13:44.360
This is why I love you.

309
00:13:44.560 --> 00:13:45.800
Goes back so far.

310
00:13:46.060 --> 00:13:48.120
It does, but it just got me so tickled.

311
00:13:48.760 --> 00:13:52.360
We had a fan question from KJ Davey.

312
00:13:52.680 --> 00:13:55.100
Erin is my favorite character of The Office.

313
00:13:55.320 --> 00:13:59.100
How did the producers come up with her personality and her character as a whole?

314
00:13:59.100 --> 00:14:04.060
And how much creative liberty did Ellie have in creating her character's quirks and traits?

315
00:14:04.460 --> 00:14:11.460
KJ, Gene told me something crazy about the development of the character of Kelly Aaron.

316
00:14:12.100 --> 00:14:19.820
He said that the writers had not fully fleshed out Aaron's personality by the time we started shooting.

317
00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:28.440
So when we started, they had Ellie perform all of her scenes and all of her talking heads two different ways.

318
00:14:29.100 --> 00:14:30.700
As two different characters.

319
00:14:30.960 --> 00:14:31.840
I remember this.

320
00:14:32.120 --> 00:14:36.700
She had to do them in like that earnest, quirky way that we know and love as Aaron.

321
00:14:36.880 --> 00:14:38.460
That's the one we eventually go with.

322
00:14:38.820 --> 00:14:46.860
But Gene said, believe it or not, there exists a bizarro Aaron where her lines are also delivered in a no-nonsense way.

323
00:14:47.960 --> 00:14:52.720
And I asked him, how long did she have to do this before they decided?

324
00:14:53.360 --> 00:15:01.380
And he said they definitely had like two totally different versions of her talking heads written.

325
00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:09.100
And then in her scenes with Dwight and Andy hitting on her, she had to then perform those with different characteristics.

326
00:15:10.320 --> 00:15:15.180
I mean, Gene said he gives her so much credit because this was her first big role on a TV show.

327
00:15:15.180 --> 00:15:19.160
And she basically did two versions of Aaron in every scene for the entire week.

328
00:15:19.160 --> 00:15:23.440
So until you shared about that sort of two versions of Aaron, I had forgotten about it.

329
00:15:23.560 --> 00:15:25.940
But now there's a deleted scene that makes sense to me.

330
00:15:26.640 --> 00:15:27.720
Aaron just looks at camera.

331
00:15:28.020 --> 00:15:29.600
You know, she's doing a talking head.

332
00:15:29.760 --> 00:15:33.020
