1000
00:48:20.560 --> 00:48:27.720
And he said, I mean, how hard is it to make good coffee and eggs, really?

1001
00:48:28.220 --> 00:48:29.160
Oh, no.

1002
00:48:29.420 --> 00:48:37.220
I feel like maybe you're just complimenting my coffee and eggs so that I make you coffee and eggs every day.

1003
00:48:38.200 --> 00:48:42.520
And I was like, no, they really are superior.

1004
00:48:42.520 --> 00:48:45.280
I swear it's better coffee than I make.

1005
00:48:45.280 --> 00:48:52.220
I mean, that we could prove because there were some mornings when I made the coffee and Lee was like, oh, yeah, that's not great.

1006
00:48:52.320 --> 00:48:54.040
But Lee doesn't eat eggs.

1007
00:48:54.200 --> 00:48:57.460
I eat eggs in the morning and he would always make me my eggs.

1008
00:48:57.520 --> 00:48:59.020
But it's the truth, babe.

1009
00:48:59.460 --> 00:49:01.980
Lee, you make the best coffee and eggs.

1010
00:49:02.160 --> 00:49:03.280
You just do.

1011
00:49:04.120 --> 00:49:07.640
Lee, I've traveled only a handful of times with your wife.

1012
00:49:07.860 --> 00:49:10.320
I know you have traveled with her many, many times.

1013
00:49:11.100 --> 00:49:14.520
And I know that this woman does not lie about food or beverage.

1014
00:49:14.520 --> 00:49:15.380
Thank you.

1015
00:49:15.800 --> 00:49:18.540
She is completely earnest when she likes something.

1016
00:49:18.660 --> 00:49:20.500
And when she doesn't, you're going to know about it.

1017
00:49:20.680 --> 00:49:21.420
That's the thing.

1018
00:49:21.580 --> 00:49:28.020
I'm not going to eat mediocre eggs for five years just because someone else made them for me.

1019
00:49:28.060 --> 00:49:32.200
I mean, if I really believed I could make better eggs, I'd be making my own eggs.

1020
00:49:32.300 --> 00:49:32.560
Oh, yeah.

1021
00:49:32.760 --> 00:49:38.540
Well, once again, while people are talking in Michael Scott Paper Company, you hear someone in the bathroom.

1022
00:49:38.880 --> 00:49:42.140
Yeah, you hear their voice through the ceiling.

1023
00:49:42.140 --> 00:49:44.080
You hear them peeing.

1024
00:49:44.440 --> 00:49:47.060
We had a fan question from Afrin R.

1025
00:49:47.400 --> 00:49:54.920
In the scene where Michael, Pam, and Ryan are in their small new office and we hear a male voice talking on his phone in the bathroom.

1026
00:49:55.060 --> 00:49:55.920
Whose voice is it?

1027
00:49:56.020 --> 00:49:59.540
It sounds like Toby, but the conversation made me doubt it.

1028
00:49:59.960 --> 00:50:01.280
It was Toby.

1029
00:50:01.900 --> 00:50:02.960
Paul did the voice.

1030
00:50:02.960 --> 00:50:10.180
Now, on the commentary, I think Gene and Lee joked that they made Paul sit up in the ceiling tiles to do his lines.

1031
00:50:10.940 --> 00:50:12.060
But that is not true.

1032
00:50:12.260 --> 00:50:14.140
He was actually just off camera.

1033
00:50:14.140 --> 00:50:15.320
He was not in the ceiling.

1034
00:50:15.720 --> 00:50:22.240
They added all the effects in post to make it sound like he was in the bathroom above us, including, like, all the peeing sounds.

1035
00:50:22.380 --> 00:50:24.360
But it really sounds like he's above you.

1036
00:50:24.460 --> 00:50:26.440
I mean, I was so sold on that.

1037
00:50:26.600 --> 00:50:26.820
Yeah.

1038
00:50:26.820 --> 00:50:27.920
No, he was not.

1039
00:50:28.120 --> 00:50:29.140
He was just off camera.

1040
00:50:29.440 --> 00:50:41.040
But incidentally, I would like to point out that our sound team was nominated for an Emmy for Outstanding Sound Mixing for a Comedy or Drama Series Half Hour for this episode.

1041
00:50:41.240 --> 00:50:42.320
Well, they deserve it.

1042
00:50:42.420 --> 00:50:42.840
I know.

1043
00:50:42.940 --> 00:50:44.680
It really sounded like he was up there.

1044
00:50:44.780 --> 00:50:46.220
And all the flushing and everything.

1045
00:50:47.200 --> 00:50:52.620
Well, Michael's going to call his mom and talk in code, Jenna, much in the way that you and I talk in code.

1046
00:50:52.760 --> 00:50:53.780
He's really bad at it.

1047
00:50:54.000 --> 00:50:54.900
It's so obvious.

1048
00:50:55.080 --> 00:50:55.600
It's so obvious.

1049
00:50:55.800 --> 00:50:58.020
He says, Mom, they're getting on my nerves.

1050
00:50:58.240 --> 00:50:59.580
R thinks he's too good to be here.

1051
00:50:59.680 --> 00:51:01.660
And P is not as much fun without Jim.

1052
00:51:02.120 --> 00:51:04.140
And then he's like, Mom, I got to go.

1053
00:51:04.280 --> 00:51:05.440
P's being a giant bee.

1054
00:51:06.140 --> 00:51:07.260
This is us, lady.

1055
00:51:07.640 --> 00:51:13.800
Well, this whole thing is going to end with Pam and Ryan bickering over the computer.

1056
00:51:13.800 --> 00:51:17.500
I mean, they get in a huge fight over who gets to use it.

1057
00:51:17.940 --> 00:51:24.120
And at eight minutes and 20 seconds at the end of this scene, the camera pushes in on Michael.

1058
00:51:24.600 --> 00:51:26.300
He's standing in front of the whiteboard.

1059
00:51:26.560 --> 00:51:33.380
And written on the whiteboard is a quote that says, you miss 100% of the shots.

1060
00:51:33.660 --> 00:51:34.300
You don't take.

1061
00:51:34.600 --> 00:51:36.920
Wayne Gretzky, Michael Scott.

1062
00:51:38.360 --> 00:51:41.100
As if Wayne Gretzky is part of the quote.

1063
00:51:41.380 --> 00:51:41.940
Yes.

1064
00:51:42.280 --> 00:51:42.460
Right?

1065
00:51:42.460 --> 00:51:46.940
Michael Scott is quoting himself, quoting Wayne Gretzky.

1066
00:51:47.480 --> 00:51:49.500
Justin Spitzer wrote that joke.

1067
00:51:50.060 --> 00:51:54.820
Gene and Lee both brought it up, saying it was one of their favorite parts of the episode.

1068
00:51:55.160 --> 00:51:57.500
Like, I see that meme all the time.

1069
00:51:57.720 --> 00:51:58.280
Oh, yeah.

1070
00:51:58.460 --> 00:51:59.180
It's so brilliant.

1071
00:51:59.400 --> 00:52:06.600
If you Google Wayne Gretzky's quote, a Michael Scott version with his picture comes up.

1072
00:52:06.700 --> 00:52:07.220
It's crazy.

1073
00:52:07.220 --> 00:52:09.020
Well, why don't we take a break?

1074
00:52:09.240 --> 00:52:21.480
And when we come back, we still have to discuss the pancake luncheon and Dwight and Andy's rivalry and Jim maybe finally figuring out what a rundown is.

1075
00:52:21.620 --> 00:52:25.200
And also a scene where maybe Jim has disappeared.

1076
00:52:25.580 --> 00:52:26.540
Where has he gone?

1077
00:52:26.540 --> 00:52:27.920
And you might have the answer.

1078
00:52:28.160 --> 00:52:28.760
Oh, wow.

1079
00:52:28.980 --> 00:52:31.080
Oh, I also have a sunglasses thing.

1080
00:52:31.320 --> 00:52:32.700
Oh, and I do too.

1081
00:52:32.940 --> 00:52:34.620
There's so much to come back for.

1082
00:52:44.030 --> 00:52:44.890
We're back.

1083
00:52:45.350 --> 00:52:50.450
Dwight is going to approach Andy about his obvious attraction to Aaron.

1084
00:52:50.450 --> 00:52:56.530
And only a way that Dwight would, about tingly feelings and blood flow to places.

1085
00:52:57.490 --> 00:52:57.750
Yes.

1086
00:52:58.030 --> 00:53:02.770
But he also confesses that he has his own feelings for Aaron.

1087
00:53:03.370 --> 00:53:03.770
Mm-hmm.

1088
00:53:04.210 --> 00:53:08.130
And they sort of talk about like, no, no, no, I don't want to get in your way and vice versa.

1089
00:53:08.350 --> 00:53:08.610
Mm-hmm.

1090
00:53:08.610 --> 00:53:18.370
I want you to note at 9 minutes, 28 seconds, while Dwight and Andy are talking, Aaron is in the background directly in the middle of these two guys.

1091
00:53:18.930 --> 00:53:20.690
Oh, I'm sure that was on purpose.

1092
00:53:21.010 --> 00:53:21.750
Oh, it was.

1093
00:53:21.950 --> 00:53:23.730
Gene and Lee said that was intentional.

1094
00:53:24.250 --> 00:53:32.010
They said they did this as many times as they could in this episode because it is a story about a woman coming between two guys.

1095
00:53:32.470 --> 00:53:38.370
I really loved Leslie's look in the background as well.

1096
00:53:38.370 --> 00:53:40.270
There's a lot to see in the background of this scene.

1097
00:53:40.390 --> 00:53:41.010
That's pretty great.

1098
00:53:41.230 --> 00:53:44.110
And there's also someone missing in the background of this scene.

1099
00:53:44.970 --> 00:53:45.970
Where is Jim?

1100
00:53:46.390 --> 00:53:47.250
Mm-hmm.

1101
00:53:47.650 --> 00:53:49.110
I can tell you where he was.

1102
00:53:49.250 --> 00:53:49.910
Where was he?

1103
00:53:50.170 --> 00:53:54.250
They shared in the commentary that John had to leave early to be on The Tonight Show.

1104
00:53:54.450 --> 00:53:55.550
Oh, my gosh.

1105
00:53:56.790 --> 00:54:04.310
Well, you know, we were rapidly approaching our 100th episode of The Office, which is going to be Company Picnic, the finale of Season 5.

1106
00:54:04.610 --> 00:54:08.050
And we were starting to do a lot of press and promotion for that.

1107
00:54:08.370 --> 00:54:20.390
I saw on the call sheets that after work on Thursday of this week, me and John and Rain stayed after work, and we shot some syndicated promos.

1108
00:54:21.230 --> 00:54:21.710
Oh, yeah.

1109
00:54:22.110 --> 00:54:26.830
I found some old emails that a few of us did a satellite media tour as well.

1110
00:54:26.990 --> 00:54:27.510
I bet.

1111
00:54:27.510 --> 00:54:27.850
Yeah.

1112
00:54:28.110 --> 00:54:34.370
I always got roped in for those, and they started at 4 in the morning because you do East Coast to West CoaSt.

1113
00:54:34.650 --> 00:54:35.950
We were very excited.

1114
00:54:35.950 --> 00:54:37.110
We were happy to do it.

1115
00:54:37.210 --> 00:54:38.110
We were team players.

1116
00:54:38.390 --> 00:54:40.710
I was always really proud of our group effort for the show.

1117
00:54:41.930 --> 00:54:48.430
Well, Jim is going to reappear pretty quickly because he's asking Oscar what the rundown is, right?

1118
00:54:48.570 --> 00:54:48.790
Mm-hmm.

1119
00:54:48.790 --> 00:54:52.290
He's gone over to the accounting nook much of the way that Michael used to do.

1120
00:54:52.290 --> 00:54:57.330
He would go ask Oscar what something meant, and now Jim is doing it.

1121
00:54:57.450 --> 00:55:00.230
I mean, Oscar's kind of the smartest guy in the office.

1122
00:55:00.450 --> 00:55:05.010
Jenna, I love that you said that because Justin Spitzer said this in the commentary.

1123
00:55:05.270 --> 00:55:08.730
He joked that Oscar was the voice of the writers.

1124
00:55:09.070 --> 00:55:12.190
He's the smartest guy who's always judging everyone.

1125
00:55:15.680 --> 00:55:16.800
Yeah, 100%.

1126
00:55:16.800 --> 00:55:19.320
But Oscar says, why don't you just ask him?

1127
00:55:19.500 --> 00:55:22.060
Just ask Charles what the rundown is.

1128
00:55:22.920 --> 00:55:27.860
So there was a deleted scene where Jim actually took Oscar's advice.

1129
00:55:28.060 --> 00:55:28.240
What?

1130
00:55:28.560 --> 00:55:28.940
Yeah.

1131
00:55:29.240 --> 00:55:30.180
You've got to hear it.

1132
00:55:32.860 --> 00:55:33.300
You have a second?

1133
00:55:33.860 --> 00:55:34.560
What is it, Jim?

1134
00:55:34.820 --> 00:55:36.020
It's about the rundown.

1135
00:55:36.400 --> 00:55:40.840
Jim, God, this rundown is taking more of my time than if I did it myself.

1136
00:55:40.840 --> 00:55:41.280
What?

1137
00:55:41.920 --> 00:55:43.280
What is the question now?

1138
00:55:44.080 --> 00:55:45.020
What's a rundown?

1139
00:55:47.200 --> 00:55:48.440
Is this one of your pranks?

1140
00:55:52.420 --> 00:55:52.940
Huh?

1141
00:55:54.660 --> 00:55:55.020
Yep.

1142
00:55:57.000 --> 00:55:57.360
Boom.

1143
00:55:57.620 --> 00:55:57.800
Jim.

1144
00:55:58.100 --> 00:55:58.380
Sorry.

1145
00:55:58.560 --> 00:55:59.080
I don't have time.

1146
00:55:59.180 --> 00:55:59.400
I know.

1147
00:55:59.540 --> 00:55:59.720
Okay.

1148
00:55:59.900 --> 00:56:00.120
All right.

1149
00:56:00.380 --> 00:56:01.340
I'm going to get you that rundown.

1150
00:56:01.340 --> 00:56:02.000
Just give it to me, Jim.

1151
00:56:02.140 --> 00:56:02.440
Right now.

1152
00:56:02.700 --> 00:56:05.200
I'm going to go out and find it.

1153
00:56:06.140 --> 00:56:07.320
Oh, my gosh.

1154
00:56:07.560 --> 00:56:08.500
Isn't that amazing?

1155
00:56:08.920 --> 00:56:13.660
And I love that Charles clearly knows that Jim's the prankster, which he probably, you

1156
00:56:13.660 --> 00:56:16.320
know, just add that to the list of things he doesn't like about Jim.

1157
00:56:16.720 --> 00:56:19.900
But Jim actually asked him and then bailed.

1158
00:56:20.800 --> 00:56:22.380
I bet that was a really funny scene.

1159
00:56:22.400 --> 00:56:23.440
I wish that had stayed in.

1160
00:56:23.940 --> 00:56:24.400
It was great.

1161
00:56:24.500 --> 00:56:27.420
There was so much awkward, just long pauses.

1162
00:56:27.760 --> 00:56:27.960
Oh.

1163
00:56:28.580 --> 00:56:33.300
Well, back downstairs, Michael determines that their office space is too small.

1164
00:56:34.200 --> 00:56:38.280
He says that the solution is for Pam and Ryan to each choose a corner.

1165
00:56:38.800 --> 00:56:40.820
Pam suggests they work from home.

1166
00:56:41.140 --> 00:56:44.500
Ryan suggests Michael fire whichever of them has less education.

1167
00:56:44.840 --> 00:56:47.200
There's a little bit of that passive aggressive.

1168
00:56:47.200 --> 00:56:50.820
But Michael is like, no, my corner idea is what it is.

1169
00:56:51.120 --> 00:56:57.560
I want you to know there was a talking head in the script where Michael says that he negotiated

1170
00:56:57.560 --> 00:56:59.640
a seven-year lease on this space.

1171
00:56:59.640 --> 00:57:00.160
No.

1172
00:57:01.580 --> 00:57:02.220
No.

1173
00:57:02.740 --> 00:57:03.660
But it gets worse.

1174
00:57:03.960 --> 00:57:07.540
He says, originally, Billy started at three years.

1175
00:57:07.760 --> 00:57:09.640
Michael countered with seven.

1176
00:57:09.780 --> 00:57:10.780
No, Michael.

1177
00:57:11.140 --> 00:57:13.260
And then Michael says, I should have said 10.

1178
00:57:13.900 --> 00:57:15.040
Oh, my gosh.

1179
00:57:15.040 --> 00:57:18.840
So, this is going to be their space for seven years.

1180
00:57:19.540 --> 00:57:21.100
Oh, my gosh.

1181
00:57:21.600 --> 00:57:23.120
Justin pointed out something really funny.

1182
00:57:23.300 --> 00:57:26.960
He was like, you know, when Michael says, there are four corners in this room.

1183
00:57:27.100 --> 00:57:27.300
Yeah.

1184
00:57:27.580 --> 00:57:29.600
And you guys kind of look to camera like, yeah, idiot.

1185
00:57:30.420 --> 00:57:32.440
Actually, there were more than four.

1186
00:57:32.720 --> 00:57:36.480
There were because there were some, like, weird bumpy things.

1187
00:57:38.380 --> 00:57:40.780
Well, Pam is going to retreat to her corner.

1188
00:57:41.000 --> 00:57:45.680
By the way, her corner is next to the sewage pipe and the shower.

1189
00:57:45.900 --> 00:57:47.120
Facing a wall.

1190
00:57:47.300 --> 00:57:49.060
You'd think it can't get worse.

1191
00:57:49.600 --> 00:57:52.420
Ryan's corner is, like, behind a plant.

1192
00:57:52.420 --> 00:57:55.120
It's actually kind of the nicest corner, really.

1193
00:57:55.880 --> 00:57:59.460
But things are going to get worse for Pam because Michael says that's his corner.

1194
00:57:59.600 --> 00:58:03.420
Because he can't work in the same corner that he relaxes in.

1195
00:58:03.520 --> 00:58:03.720
Right.

1196
00:58:04.040 --> 00:58:05.480
So, she's like, which one's mine?

1197
00:58:05.500 --> 00:58:07.640
And he says, yours is the one over there.

1198
00:58:07.880 --> 00:58:09.220
By the copier.

1199
00:58:09.380 --> 00:58:09.740
Oh.

1200
00:58:09.980 --> 00:58:14.040
We had a fan catch at 12 minutes, one second.

1201
00:58:14.320 --> 00:58:16.600
And it's a great continuity catch.

1202
00:58:16.600 --> 00:58:17.720
It's very subtle.

1203
00:58:18.040 --> 00:58:25.240
So, hats off to Tatiana V, who says, when Pam goes to sit in her corner, she takes a small

1204
00:58:25.240 --> 00:58:26.760
black object with her.

1205
00:58:26.760 --> 00:58:31.660
You can see her holding it in her lap as the camera swings back and forth from her and

1206
00:58:31.660 --> 00:58:32.020
Michael.

1207
00:58:33.620 --> 00:58:39.600
But, right before she gets up to leave, it has disappeared from her hands because Pam

1208
00:58:39.600 --> 00:58:41.660
is now holding the arms of her chair.

1209
00:58:41.980 --> 00:58:42.860
What is it?

1210
00:58:43.080 --> 00:58:44.580
That's what she wanted to know.

1211
00:58:44.760 --> 00:58:46.700
It was Pam's flip phone.

1212
00:58:47.160 --> 00:58:52.620
Pam grabs her flip phone off of the poker table, but clearly I didn't do it in every take

1213
00:58:52.620 --> 00:58:54.580
because it does just vanish.

1214
00:58:55.180 --> 00:58:56.460
I miss my flip phone.

1215
00:58:57.140 --> 00:58:57.760
You do?

1216
00:58:57.960 --> 00:58:58.380
I do.

1217
00:58:58.500 --> 00:59:02.980
And I miss the little antenna it had and how I would close the antenna with my chin.

1218
00:59:03.160 --> 00:59:04.620
I'd like shove it into my chin.

1219
00:59:05.180 --> 00:59:06.720
It did feel fun.

1220
00:59:07.000 --> 00:59:07.840
I loved it.

1221
00:59:07.980 --> 00:59:08.030
The flip phone.

1222
00:59:08.180 --> 00:59:08.340
Yeah.

1223
00:59:08.840 --> 00:59:13.820
Well, you know, Samsung has a new flip phone thing where you flip it open and it becomes

1224
00:59:13.820 --> 00:59:14.820
like a big screen.

1225
00:59:14.820 --> 00:59:16.260
Have you seen the commercials for it?

1226
00:59:16.260 --> 00:59:17.420
I'll never be able to figure it out.

1227
00:59:17.580 --> 00:59:18.540
There's too many moving parts.

1228
00:59:18.540 --> 00:59:20.540
I know, but it looks cool in the commercials.

1229
00:59:20.540 --> 00:59:21.760
It really does, Samsung.

1230
00:59:22.280 --> 00:59:24.400
You know what I don't miss about my flip phone, lady?

1231
00:59:24.660 --> 00:59:24.920
What?

1232
00:59:25.160 --> 00:59:28.300
I don't miss the texting where you had to...

1233
00:59:28.300 --> 00:59:31.460
A-A-B-B-C-C-D-E-E.

1234
00:59:31.600 --> 00:59:32.820
Like you had to click, click, click.

1235
00:59:32.880 --> 00:59:32.930
Yeah.

1236
00:59:34.060 --> 00:59:40.820
Listen, all of this business with Ryan and the corners, Pam's going to leave.

1237
00:59:41.080 --> 00:59:45.060
She goes upstairs and she asks Charles for her old job back.

1238
00:59:45.280 --> 00:59:47.380
She doesn't consult her fiance.

1239
00:59:48.100 --> 00:59:50.380
Not that she needs to consult him, but you know what I mean?

1240
00:59:50.400 --> 00:59:51.680
You would think she'd loop him in.

1241
00:59:51.820 --> 00:59:54.820
You'd think she'd like say, Jim, I'm going to ask for my job back.

1242
00:59:55.160 --> 00:59:59.160
But she didn't consult him when she quit and she's not going to consult him now.

1243
00:59:59.380 --> 01:00:00.160
She's desperate.

1244
01:00:00.340 --> 01:00:01.800
She doesn't have time for that conversation.

1245
01:00:02.020 --> 01:00:02.160
No.

1246
01:00:02.760 --> 01:00:04.700
Well, Charles says the position has been filled.

1247
01:00:05.100 --> 01:00:06.820
She says maybe a sales job.

1248
01:00:07.120 --> 01:00:10.360
Maybe a job as his personal assistant, personal shopper.

1249
01:00:11.300 --> 01:00:11.700
Nope.

1250
01:00:12.160 --> 01:00:12.860
No dice.

1251
01:00:12.860 --> 01:00:20.300
So Justin talked about several different alts in the scene where they had Charles be really

1252
01:00:20.300 --> 01:00:26.380
sort of abrupt with Pam and they dialed it back because it seemed too harsh.

1253
01:00:26.560 --> 01:00:27.760
So he's just more indifferent.

1254
01:00:28.040 --> 01:00:28.820
He's just more business.

1255
01:00:29.560 --> 01:00:29.720
Yeah.

1256
01:00:29.940 --> 01:00:36.260
Well, this was my only real one-on-one scene with Idris, except for when he sort of came in

1257
01:00:36.260 --> 01:00:38.640
the first day, but that wasn't much of an exchange.

1258
01:00:39.400 --> 01:00:40.740
I was so nervous.

1259
01:00:41.540 --> 01:00:42.780
I was such a fan.

1260
01:00:43.600 --> 01:00:49.620
And to be standing there with this actor that I admired so much, because I was a huge fan of The Wire.

1261
01:00:49.880 --> 01:00:54.360
And he has such a patient, quiet power in his scenes.

1262
01:00:54.460 --> 01:00:54.720
Mm-hmm.

1263
01:00:55.180 --> 01:00:56.540
And he's such a pro.

1264
01:00:56.540 --> 01:01:04.720
So, I mean, I was just, I think some of my nervousness as Pam was just my nervousness as

1265
01:01:04.720 --> 01:01:07.120
Jenna performing with this person that I admired.

1266
01:01:07.500 --> 01:01:07.720
Yeah.

1267
01:01:08.220 --> 01:01:12.420
Word has clearly gotten out about the Michael Scott Paper Company being downstairs, because

1268
01:01:12.420 --> 01:01:16.240
Phyllis and Stanley decide to go pop by and say hi.

1269
01:01:16.360 --> 01:01:17.500
We really know what it was.

1270
01:01:17.640 --> 01:01:18.560
They were just snooping.

1271
01:01:19.220 --> 01:01:20.060
Oh, yeah.

1272
01:01:20.160 --> 01:01:20.320
Yeah.

1273
01:01:20.440 --> 01:01:21.320
I would do the same thing.

1274
01:01:21.320 --> 01:01:21.840
Are you kidding?

1275
01:01:21.840 --> 01:01:28.720
Well, at the top of the scene, when Phyllis and Stanley poked their head in, I want you

1276
01:01:28.720 --> 01:01:31.960
