1277
01:01:32.560 --> 01:01:36.880
The stapler that we loved, that none of us could keep our hands off of.

1278
01:01:37.020 --> 01:01:41.940
We would seriously staple papers on our desk.

1279
01:01:42.060 --> 01:01:45.520
So, do you think Steve was just, like, playing with the stapler he thought was cool?

1280
01:01:46.020 --> 01:01:50.500
Because I don't know how to explain this air pressure mechanism of the stapler.

1281
01:01:50.500 --> 01:01:53.640
Okay, next time I'm over at your house, will you just show me the stapler?

1282
01:01:53.780 --> 01:01:56.160
I seriously should have brought it in, because you can hear it.

1283
01:01:56.240 --> 01:01:57.180
It's like, ka-chunk.

1284
01:01:57.680 --> 01:01:58.000
Wow.

1285
01:01:58.180 --> 01:02:01.940
It's like having all the power of an industrial stapler.

1286
01:02:02.220 --> 01:02:03.760
In the palm of your hand.

1287
01:02:03.880 --> 01:02:05.460
You should do commercials for them.

1288
01:02:05.640 --> 01:02:06.440
I really should.

1289
01:02:06.540 --> 01:02:07.800
They should sponsor us.

1290
01:02:07.980 --> 01:02:09.560
It's just the push of your finger.

1291
01:02:09.700 --> 01:02:15.800
And when you do it, it's such an engineering marvel that you just want to staple everything

1292
01:02:15.800 --> 01:02:16.360
in sight.

1293
01:02:16.500 --> 01:02:17.160
Well, good Lord.

1294
01:02:17.240 --> 01:02:19.000
I need to see the stapler.

1295
01:02:19.420 --> 01:02:22.300
Maybe I should do a video of myself stapling things.

1296
01:02:22.320 --> 01:02:22.560
Would you please?

1297
01:02:22.560 --> 01:02:25.140
And you can put it in the office of these Instagram stories.

1298
01:02:25.160 --> 01:02:25.880
Give it to me.

1299
01:02:26.040 --> 01:02:27.040
We all need to see it.

1300
01:02:27.100 --> 01:02:28.140
Okay, I'll do it.

1301
01:02:28.280 --> 01:02:29.620
I need to hold it in my hand.

1302
01:02:29.620 --> 01:02:30.500
I need to touch it.

1303
01:02:30.640 --> 01:02:31.180
Wait a second.

1304
01:02:31.320 --> 01:02:31.620
Wait a second.

1305
01:02:31.620 --> 01:02:33.840
That is what she said.

1306
01:02:34.280 --> 01:02:37.040
The minute I started going down that road, I was like, no, back up.

1307
01:02:37.040 --> 01:02:37.940
Wow.

1308
01:02:38.620 --> 01:02:40.020
Moving us along.

1309
01:02:40.240 --> 01:02:45.680
Lady, it is time to kick off this pancake luncheon.

1310
01:02:46.140 --> 01:02:47.400
Michael is outside.

1311
01:02:47.400 --> 01:02:50.880
He is making square pancakes for nobody yet.

1312
01:02:51.160 --> 01:02:52.300
Ryan is texting.

1313
01:02:52.480 --> 01:02:54.840
I love that Michael's like, stop with the texting machine.

1314
01:02:54.840 --> 01:02:55.600
Mm-hmm.

1315
01:02:57.420 --> 01:03:02.780
So here we are, Jenna, at our second pair of sunglasses at 14 minutes, 59 seconds.

1316
01:03:03.040 --> 01:03:03.600
Oh, yes.

1317
01:03:03.740 --> 01:03:05.280
I have the same time code.

1318
01:03:05.620 --> 01:03:08.040
What do you want to say about these sunglasses?

1319
01:03:08.460 --> 01:03:10.220
Wait, can we say it right at the same time?

1320
01:03:10.380 --> 01:03:12.600
It'll be jarbled, but let's see if it sounds the same.

1321
01:03:12.700 --> 01:03:12.980
Okay.

1322
01:03:12.980 --> 01:03:23.120
These sunglasses were inspired by Joaquin Phoenix's appearance on The David Letterman Show in 2009

1323
01:03:23.120 --> 01:03:25.420
when he was promoting I'm Still Here.

1324
01:03:25.880 --> 01:03:27.340
It was a very odd appearance.

1325
01:03:27.340 --> 01:03:32.760
I watched that in real time, but it was all part of like a marketing ploy or something.

1326
01:03:32.960 --> 01:03:40.680
He did this film, and I guess he was trying to make us believe that he had actually switched

1327
01:03:40.680 --> 01:03:45.040
careers, and it was sort of like an Andy Kaufman-esque thing.

1328
01:03:45.500 --> 01:03:46.740
I took a screen grab.

1329
01:03:47.040 --> 01:03:50.360
I did a side-by-side for you, lady.

1330
01:03:50.660 --> 01:03:51.920
Oh, give it to me.

1331
01:03:52.060 --> 01:03:55.200
Joaquin Phoenix and Ryan, same sunglasses.

1332
01:03:55.660 --> 01:03:56.720
Putting that in stories.

1333
01:03:56.980 --> 01:03:58.980
They retail for about $400.

1334
01:03:59.580 --> 01:03:59.940
What?

1335
01:04:00.200 --> 01:04:01.240
For sunglasses?

1336
01:04:01.700 --> 01:04:01.920
Yeah.

1337
01:04:02.520 --> 01:04:03.260
Are you crazy?

1338
01:04:03.400 --> 01:04:04.140
Are they prescription?

1339
01:04:04.560 --> 01:04:05.980
No, they're just fancy.

1340
01:04:06.120 --> 01:04:06.740
That's nuts.

1341
01:04:06.740 --> 01:04:12.340
I mean, if I bought that pair of sunglasses, I might as well just flush $400 down the toilet

1342
01:04:12.340 --> 01:04:14.120
because I'm going to lose them in less than a year.

1343
01:04:14.340 --> 01:04:18.940
I know some people like fancy sunglasses, and listen, you do you, but I don't know.

1344
01:04:19.120 --> 01:04:22.920
Three kids, sunglasses, soccer games, mine just get wrecked.

1345
01:04:23.300 --> 01:04:28.300
I splurged on a pair of $200 prescription sunglasses.

1346
01:04:28.300 --> 01:04:30.120
I have to have prescription sunglasses.

1347
01:04:30.120 --> 01:04:34.600
Because I was doing the double glasses for so long, you know, where you buy a giant pair

1348
01:04:34.600 --> 01:04:37.960
of regular sunglasses that you put over your real glasses.

1349
01:04:38.220 --> 01:04:38.680
I saw it, Jenna.

1350
01:04:38.780 --> 01:04:41.540
You look like you need to live in like a Florida retirement community.

1351
01:04:41.980 --> 01:04:42.120
I know.

1352
01:04:42.260 --> 01:04:43.200
And you know what?

1353
01:04:43.340 --> 01:04:48.040
I managed to keep those prescription sunglasses for almost two years.

1354
01:04:49.040 --> 01:04:53.080
I lost them somewhere, and now I'm back to double glasses.

1355
01:04:53.700 --> 01:04:55.000
You know what we need?

1356
01:04:55.180 --> 01:04:55.460
What?

1357
01:04:55.760 --> 01:04:58.440
Josh says I need the chain on my glasses.

1358
01:04:59.060 --> 01:05:00.780
Oh, I have a story about my mom.

1359
01:05:00.940 --> 01:05:01.640
What happens?

1360
01:05:01.740 --> 01:05:02.440
That's it, right?

1361
01:05:02.540 --> 01:05:03.000
That's it.

1362
01:05:03.080 --> 01:05:04.300
Your sexy days are over.

1363
01:05:04.460 --> 01:05:06.520
If you put your glasses on a chain, I don't know.

1364
01:05:06.660 --> 01:05:12.520
Well, my mom, we affectionately call her Lucy because when you go into a store with her,

1365
01:05:12.740 --> 01:05:18.400
it's like you're shopping with Lucille Ball from I Love Lucy because she will manage to

1366
01:05:18.400 --> 01:05:22.580
get tangled in or knock over any store display.

1367
01:05:22.780 --> 01:05:26.480
I was going to say, does she knock things over or try to put too many chocolates in her mouth?

1368
01:05:26.480 --> 01:05:33.500
Well, so we were shopping with her, and she had on her glasses around one of those chains,

1369
01:05:34.060 --> 01:05:39.860
but it was winter, so she also had a scarf, and she also had, I don't know why, like long

1370
01:05:39.860 --> 01:05:43.060
necklaces, a purse, you know, cross-bodied.

1371
01:05:43.520 --> 01:05:47.640
She goes to take off her cross-body purse.

1372
01:05:47.900 --> 01:05:50.500
It yanks on her sunglasses chain.

1373
01:05:50.800 --> 01:05:52.080
Elbows are flying.

1374
01:05:52.300 --> 01:05:55.060
She takes down a whole display of earrings.

1375
01:05:55.460 --> 01:05:55.920
Oh, no.

1376
01:05:55.920 --> 01:06:00.560
My sister and I are, like, rushing in to, like, help her.

1377
01:06:00.660 --> 01:06:01.460
She's tangled.

1378
01:06:01.700 --> 01:06:07.280
She looks like a cat tangled in string, and just displays are falling down.

1379
01:06:07.780 --> 01:06:14.300
So whenever I think about putting my glasses on a chain, that memory comes back to me,

1380
01:06:14.320 --> 01:06:16.060
and I think, that could be me.

1381
01:06:16.380 --> 01:06:17.580
I could be that.

1382
01:06:17.700 --> 01:06:19.280
I could easily have done that.

1383
01:06:19.580 --> 01:06:20.740
I could take down a display.

1384
01:06:21.220 --> 01:06:22.560
You could take down a display.

1385
01:06:22.840 --> 01:06:26.320
I saw you almost take out a few people on an airplane with a guitar.

1386
01:06:26.860 --> 01:06:27.200
Yeah.

1387
01:06:27.560 --> 01:06:27.820
Yeah.

1388
01:06:28.300 --> 01:06:32.520
I mean, so I can't, I can't chain my glasses, is the bottom line.

1389
01:06:32.580 --> 01:06:33.060
Oh, well.

1390
01:06:33.600 --> 01:06:34.300
I'm sorry.

1391
01:06:34.540 --> 01:06:34.800
Okay.

1392
01:06:34.980 --> 01:06:42.860
But we spent $400 on these glasses for the character of Ryan for this very subtle inside

1393
01:06:42.860 --> 01:06:47.040
joke that clearly Ryan is a Joaquin Phoenix fan and probably saw that.

1394
01:06:47.280 --> 01:06:48.160
It's in character.

1395
01:06:48.160 --> 01:06:51.700
He is the kind of guy who has to have the thing, the latest thing.

1396
01:06:52.140 --> 01:06:54.840
Even though his mom is driving him to work.

1397
01:06:55.040 --> 01:06:55.420
Yes.

1398
01:06:55.700 --> 01:06:56.120
Exactly.

1399
01:06:56.540 --> 01:06:57.660
He's really not employed.

1400
01:06:57.840 --> 01:06:59.080
Like, he's not earning a paycheck.

1401
01:06:59.240 --> 01:06:59.680
He isn't.

1402
01:06:59.700 --> 01:07:01.560
He's going to get $400 sunglasses.

1403
01:07:01.880 --> 01:07:08.040
At 15 minutes, 10 seconds, right as Pam is walking up, there's a great shot of some

1404
01:07:08.040 --> 01:07:09.460
fakie grocery bags.

1405
01:07:09.780 --> 01:07:10.740
Ooh, fakie bags.

1406
01:07:10.800 --> 01:07:12.160
We got some fakie bags.

1407
01:07:12.160 --> 01:07:18.120
And Jenna, you shared on the commentary something that jogged my memory.

1408
01:07:18.640 --> 01:07:21.640
It took me back immediately to this day.

1409
01:07:21.980 --> 01:07:27.660
You shared while you were filming this parking lot scene, the paparazzi snuck onto our set.

1410
01:07:27.960 --> 01:07:29.760
Oh my gosh, I remember that.

1411
01:07:29.760 --> 01:07:31.640
Yes, we had a guy.

1412
01:07:32.040 --> 01:07:33.900
So, guys, we weren't on a big lot.

1413
01:07:34.080 --> 01:07:34.960
We've shared that before.

1414
01:07:35.460 --> 01:07:36.820
We didn't have security.

1415
01:07:36.820 --> 01:07:37.900
You just drove in.

1416
01:07:38.040 --> 01:07:38.440
You did.

1417
01:07:39.000 --> 01:07:41.660
And after this day, we got a security guard.

1418
01:07:41.780 --> 01:07:42.660
In a little hut.

1419
01:07:42.900 --> 01:07:43.160
Yeah.

1420
01:07:43.320 --> 01:07:43.500
Yeah.

1421
01:07:43.800 --> 01:07:48.480
This paparazzi guy clearly staked us out, realized you could just drive right on the set,

1422
01:07:48.480 --> 01:07:54.600
came right on, and just started clicking pictures of the set, the parking lot, actors

1423
01:07:54.600 --> 01:07:55.720
